    "text": "{\"authored\":false,\"coverage\":\"explicit-paths-only; at most eight files\",\"decomposition\":[{\"status\":\"incomplete\",\"step\":\"collect_repository_evidence\"},{\"status\":\"unverified\",\"step\":\"bind_requirements_to_source\"},{\"status\":\"not_executed\",\"step\":\"implement_requested_change\"},{\"status\":\"not_executed\",\"step\":\"verify_artifact_and_requirements\"}],\"observations\":[],\"reason\":\"ReadPolicyRefused\",\"requirements\":[{\"span\":[0,9932],\"status\":\"unbound\",\"text\":\"Session stuck for 5+ hours after posting its final log: watch loop waits without limit on a HEAD workflow run held in a concurrency queue (status pending, 0 jobs); no finish/auto-continue, Telegram still shows Executing · Issue #4091 · link-assistant/hive-mind · GitHub\\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n  \\n  \\n  \\n\\n    \\n  \\n\\n\\n  \\n\\n\\n    \\n\\n\\n  \\n  \\n\\n  \\n  \\n\\n    \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n\\n  \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n    \\n\\n  \\n\\n    \\n\\n    \\n\\n      \\n\\n      \\n\\n    \\n    \\n    \\n\\n      \\n  \\n  \\n\\n\\n\\n      \\n\\n\\n\\n        \\n\\n\\n  \\n  \\n  \\n  \\n\\n  \\n\\n      \\n  \\n\\n  \\n  \\n\\n\\n\\n      \\n\\n\\n    \\n  \\n\\n\\n  \\n\\n\\n  \\n\\n  \\n  \\n\\n  \\n  \\n  \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n\\n  \\n\\n  \\n    \\n      \\n      \\n\\n    \\n      Skip to content\\n\\n      \\n    \\n      \\n      \\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n  \\n  \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n      \\n\\n        \\n            \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n  \\n  \\n\\n\\n\\n            \\n\\n                \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n  \\n  Navigation MenuSign inProductsPlatformGitHubRepository hosting, code review, and collaborationCopilotAI coding agent for tasks, projects, and automated workBuild &amp; ShipActionsCI/CD and automationCode QualityQuality analysis, fixes, and enforcementCodespacesCloud development environmentsSecureCode SecurityVulnerability detection and remediationSecret ProtectionSecret scanning and leak preventionAll FeaturesDevelopersLearnDocumentationTrainingCertificationsBuildBuild with CopilotCustomize CopilotIntegrationsExploreTrending reposGitHub SponsorsDeveloper articlesChangelogChangelogYour source for the latest features, improvements, and fixes across GitHub products, all in one place.BusinessesBy StageEnterprisesTeamStartupsNonprofitsBy IndustryHealthcareFinancial servicesManufacturingGovernmentSee all industriesEvaluate GitHubWhy GitHubCustomer StoriesBusiness insightsTrust CenterAdd-onsGitHub Advanced SecurityEnterprise-grade code securityCopilot for businessEnterprise-grade AI featuresPremium SupportEnterprise-grade 24/7 supportResourcesLearn &amp; ConnectDocumentationResource centerBlogEvents &amp; webinarsCommunity ForumCustomer StoriesIntegrationsSupportCustomer supportTrainingGitHub StatusCompanyAboutPartnersChangelogGitHub UniverseGitHub UniverseThe event for developers, by developers — talks, workshops, and what’s next for GitHub.PricingSearch/Sign inSign upAppearance settings\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n      \\n        \\n  \\n          \\n    \\n\\n          You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session.\\n          You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session.\\n          You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session.\\n\\n      \\n    \\n\\nDismiss alert\\n\\n\\n  \\n\\n    \\n\\n  \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n    \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n    \\n\\n  \\n    \\n      \\n    \\n\\n    \\n    \\n      \\n      {{ message }}\\n\\n    \\n  \\n\\n  \\n\\n\\n\\n    \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n        \\n    \\n      \\n      \\n    \\n\\n\\n    \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n    \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n  \\n  link-assistanthive-mindRepository navigationCodeIssues162 (162)Pull requests186 (186)ActionsProjectsSecurity and qualityInsightsMore items\\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n    \\n    \\n\\n\\n\\n    \\n      \\n    \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n    \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n  \\n  Session stuck for 5+ hours after posting its final log: watch loop waits without limit on a HEAD workflow run held in a concurrency queue (status pending, 0 jobs); no finish/auto-continue, Telegram still shows Executing #4091New issueCopy linkNew issueCopy linkOpen#4092OpenSession stuck for 5+ hours after posting its final log: watch loop waits without limit on a HEAD workflow run held in a concurrency queue (status pending, 0 jobs); no finish/auto-continue, Telegram still shows Executing#4091#4092Copy linkDescriptionmsidoaiopened on Nov 19, 2026Issue body actionsSummary\\nA solve run (--tool claude, model claude-opus-5-5, --think high, --attach-logs --verbose, Docker isolation, hive-mind 2.39.14) finished its AI work, uploaded its final log, and posted the \\\"🤖 Solution Draft Log … Now working session is ended\\\" comment on the pull request. It then did not exit for 5 more hours. During that time:\\n\\nthe Telegram message still said ⏳ Executing...;\\nnothing on the pull request or in Telegram said what the process was waiting for;\\nthere was no finish, no auto-continue and no auto-resume decision.\\n\\nAn operator stopped it with /stop after more than 5 hours. The kill notice then said SIGKILL; cause unknown.\\nRoot cause (high confidence, confirmed from the logs and the GitHub API): after the final log, solve went into the default --auto-restart-until-mergeable watch loop (watchUntilMergeable in src/solve.auto-merge.lib.mjs). That loop polled the PR 135 times over about 5 h 03 min. Each time it waited on one workflow run on the HEAD commit that GitHub reported as status: pending. Everything else was green:\\n\\nall 20 check runs passed (Pending: 0, Queued: 0);\\nmergeable: true, state: CLEAN.\\n\\nThe run was pending because its workflow uses a repository-wide concurrency group (cancel-in-progress: false, queue: max). Runs from other pull requests held that group, so this run waited in GitHub's concurrency queue with zero jobs. It was created about 3.5 h before the watch loop started and got its first job about 9 h after it was created, which was after the operator had already killed the session.\\ngetMergeBlockers (src/solve.auto-merge-helpers.lib.mjs, the ciStatus.status === 'success' branch) treats every non-completed workflow run on HEAD as a ci_pending blocker. This wait has no time limit of its own, the Telegram status does not show it, and nothing is posted on the PR. The only limit is the 24 h watch timeout (DEFAULT_WATCH_TIMEOUT_HOURS).\\nThis still happens on current main (2.43.3). The #4048 stuck-CI monitor (src/solve.auto-merge-stuck-ci.lib.mjs → findGhostQueuedRuns in src/github-ci-stuck-runs.lib.mjs) only looks at runs with status === 'queued'. Its comment says runs held by a concurrency group are pending and are skipped on purpose. For such a run, onPendingWorkflowRuns resets the streak and returns, so even the \\\"CI wait stuck\\\" PR notice is never posted.\\nThis is related to #4060 (queued runs on superseded commits block the AllCommits check), #4048 (ghost queued runs) and #2182 (no wall-clock limit), but it is a different case: a HEAD run in pending state held by a concurrency queue.\\nTimeline (UTC)\\n\\n\\n\\nTime\\nEvent\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n2026-11-18 07:52:07\\nDocker-isolated solve started for PR #N (hive-mind 2.39.14)\\n\\n\\n2026-11-18 07:55:55\\nClaude session started (a single long session; 15 sub-sessions, 12 sub-agent calls)\\n\\n\\n2026-11-18 21:42:21\\nLast push. GitHub creates workflow run W on HEAD. W goes straight to pending (concurrency queue), no jobs\\n\\n\\n2026-11-19 00:34:30\\n✅ Claude command completed. No processes left running … after the session. No uncommitted changes\\n\\n\\n2026-11-19 00:34:48\\n📎 Uploading log using gh-upload-log... (113 MB log). Last timestamped line of log A (log A is a snapshot taken at upload time)\\n\\n\\n00:34:48 → 01:08:40\\n34 minutes with one progress line: 🧼 Streamed sanitize: 118673213 bytes in 114 block(s). No heartbeat during the sanitize or the upload\\n\\n\\n2026-11-19 01:08:40\\n✅ Upload successful (repository, 2 chunks, 115889KB). \\\"Solution Draft Log … working session is ended\\\" comment posted\\n\\n\\n01:08:41\\n🎉 SUCCESS, then 🔄 AUTO-RESTART-UNTIL-MERGEABLE MODE ACTIVE (Watch timeout: 24 hour(s), Wait for all repo actions: No (PR-scoped CI only))\\n\\n\\n01:10:43\\n🔍 Check #1: 20/20 checks passed, mergeable: true, state: CLEAN, 1 workflow run(s) still in progress → ⏳ Waiting for CI: &lt;workflow W&gt;\\n\\n\\n01:10 → 06:13\\nChecks #2 … #135, each about 2 min 15 s apart, all identical. Telegram still shows ⏳ Executing...\\n\\n\\n~06:13:19\\nOperator /stop → [interrupt] +0ms handler entered, ⚠️ Session interrupted by user (CTRL+C), then 📎 Uploading interrupted session logs to Pull Request... (114 MB)\\n\\n\\n06:13:18–06:13:2x\\nCheck #135 still runs after the interrupt handler starts (its output is mixed with the handler's output)\\n\\n\\n06:13:29\\nContainer FinishedAt, Exit Code: 137 (SIGKILL), OOMKilled: false, cgroup oom_kill=0. This is about 10 s after CTRL+C, while the interrupted-session log upload was still sanitizing. That upload never finished\\n\\n\\n06:27:45\\nThe watcher posts \\\"📎 Intermediate working-session log (killed session)\\\". This is the start-command stdout capture (log B, 74873KB), not the solve log file\\n\\n\\n06:27:47\\n\\\"Working session was force-killed\\\" notice: exit 137, --on-session-kill=resume, \\\"This working session did not continue\\\". $ --status → exitReason = signal (SIGKILL; cause unknown)\\n\\n\\n06:41:58\\n(from the GitHub API, afterwards) The first job of workflow run W is finally created and starts on a self-hosted runner\\n\\n\\n\\nObserved vs expected\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nObserved\\nExpected\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nAfter the final log\\nProcess kept running for 5 h in a silent polling loop\\nOne of these, chosen explicitly and recorded: finish, auto-continue (restart the AI with feedback), or auto-resume. Any wait must have a reason, a deadline and a visible status\\n\\n\\nPR comment\\n\\\"Now working session is ended\\\" while the process kept going for 5 h\\nThe final comment says that monitoring continues, what it waits for and until when. Or the comment is posted only when the process really ends\\n\\n\\nTelegram\\n⏳ Executing... for 5 h\\nSomething like ⏳ Waiting for CI: workflow W pending (concurrency queue, 0 jobs) for 3h12m, check 87, gives up at HH:MM, refreshed at least every few minutes\\n\\n\\nHEAD run pending with 0 jobs, all checks green, CLEAN\\nBlocks \\\"ready to merge\\\" without limit; never reported\\nClassified as \\\"held by concurrency queue / not started\\\", logged and reported on the PR after a short threshold. After a bounded wait (configurable, much less than 24 h) the run either ends the loop with an explicit stop reason, or GitHub's CLEAN + all-green is trusted with a note on the PR\\n\\n\\n/stop\\nSIGKILL 10 s after CTRL+C, interrupted-session log upload lost, notice says cause unknown\\nEnough grace time for the interrupt handler (or a bounded, size-aware upload), and the notice says \\\"Stopped by operator (/stop)\\\" (the intent of #2052)\\n\\n\\nKill diagnostics\\nMemory, disk and cgroup readings only\"},{\"span\":[9933,16729],\"status\":\"unbound\",\"text\":\"Also the pending operation: phase watch_until_mergeable, check #135, blocker ci_pending: &lt;workflow W&gt; (pending, 0 jobs, 8.5 h), last heartbeat time\\n\\n\\n\\nEvidence (sanitized excerpts)\\nEnd of log A (the solve log file, uploaded at 00:34:48, so it cannot show what came after):\\n[2026-11-19T00:34:30.497Z] [INFO] ✅ Claude command completed\\n[2026-11-19T00:34:33.255Z] [INFO] 🔍 No processes left running in /tmp/gh-issue-solver-… after the session\\n[2026-11-19T00:34:46.081Z] [INFO] 📎 Uploading solution draft log to Pull Request...\\n[2026-11-19T00:34:46.225Z] [INFO]   📁 Large log file (113MB), will use gh-upload-log\\n[2026-11-19T00:34:48.250Z] [INFO]   🔍 Repository visibility: private, log upload will be private\\n\\nLog B (start-command stdout capture, no timestamps on solve lines), after the final upload:\\n  🧼 Streamed sanitize: 118673213 bytes in 114 block(s) (bounded worker)\\n  📤 Running: gh-upload-log /tmp/hive-mind-log-upload-XXXXXX/sanitized.log --private --description \\\"Solution draft log for &lt;PR URL&gt;\\\" --verbose\\n  ✅ Upload successful: &lt;private log repository URL&gt;\\n  📊 Type: repository, Chunks: 2\\n📈 [RESOURCES] phase=log_upload_end ts=2026-11-19T01%3A08%3A41.196Z …\\n🎉 SUCCESS: A solution draft has been prepared as a pull request\\n🔄 Auto-restart-until-mergeable mode enabled - will keep the pull request mergeable and will NOT merge it (--auto-merge merges)\\n   argv.watch (user flag): false\\n🔄 AUTO-RESTART-UNTIL-MERGEABLE MODE ACTIVE\\n   Checking interval:      120 seconds (minimum: 120s)\\n   Watch timeout:          24 hour(s)\\n   Wait for all repo actions: No (PR-scoped CI only)\\n🔍 Check #1:                 1:10:43 AM\\n[VERBOSE] /merge: PR #N detailed CI status: success\\n[VERBOSE] /merge:   Total: 20, Passed: 20, Failed: 0, Cancelled: 0, Stale: 0, Pending: 0, Queued: 0\\n[VERBOSE] /merge: Found 3 workflow run(s) for &lt;commit URL&gt;\\n[VERBOSE] /merge:   - &lt;workflow A&gt; [completed/success]: &lt;run URL&gt;\\n[VERBOSE] /merge:   - &lt;workflow W&gt; [pending]: &lt;run URL&gt;\\n[VERBOSE] /merge:   - &lt;workflow C&gt; [completed/success]: &lt;run URL&gt;\\n[VERBOSE] /merge: PR #N CI status is 'success' (20 checks passed), but 1 workflow run(s) still in progress — waiting for completion\\n[VERBOSE] /merge: PR #N mergeable: true, state: CLEAN, isDraft: false\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"&lt;full issue body JSON printed to stdout on every check&gt;\\\", …}\\n  ⏳ Waiting for CI:         &lt;workflow W&gt;\\n  ⏱️ Next check in:          120 seconds...\\n… (identical block repeated) …\\n🔍 Check #134:               6:11:46 AM\\n… identical …\\n[interrupt] +0ms handler entered\\n⚠️  Session interrupted by user (CTRL+C)\\n📎 Uploading interrupted session logs to Pull Request...\\n[interrupt] +456ms log-upload: start\\n📈 [RESOURCES] phase=log_upload_start ts=2026-11-19T06%3A13%3A19.789Z …\\n  📁 Large log file (114MB), will use gh-upload-log\\n🔍 Check #135:               6:13:18 AM          &lt;- the loop still runs after the interrupt\\n=== Container post-mortem ===\\nExit Code:  137 (SIGKILL - 128+9)\\nOOMKilled:  false\\nFinishedAt: 2026-11-19T06:13:29.352575417Z\\nMemory:     memory.max=3135369216 memory.peak=3136749568 oom=0 oom_kill=0\\n\\nGitHub API state of workflow run W (checked afterwards): event: pull_request, created_at 2026-11-18T21:42:21Z. It stayed pending until its only job was created at 2026-11-19T06:41:58Z. The workflow's concurrency is one repository-wide group with cancel-in-progress: false and queue: max. At the same time, several runs of the same workflow from other PRs were in pending or in_progress in that group. The commit-level check-runs list had no entry for W while it waited, because a run with no jobs has no check runs. That is why CheckRuns said \\\"all 20 passed\\\" while WorkflowRuns said \\\"1 in progress\\\", and nothing ever settled the disagreement.\\nNo resource problem: process RSS 283 MB, V8 heap 53 MB, cgroup 386 MB of 2.9 GB, 0 OOM kills. The cgroup memory.peak of 2.9 GB was reached hours earlier, during the AI session, and is not related to the hang.\\nRoot cause\\n\\nUnbounded wait on a pending HEAD workflow run (main bug). In src/solve.auto-merge-helpers.lib.mjs (getMergeBlockers, ciStatus.status === 'success' branch) the code does incompleteRuns = workflowRuns.filter(r =&gt; r.status !== 'completed'), and any such run becomes a ci_pending blocker. That covers pending (concurrency queue), waiting (environment approval), action_required and ghost queued runs alike. In watchUntilMergeable (src/solve.auto-merge.lib.mjs) a ci_pending blocker only logs ⏳ Waiting for CI: and sleeps. The only limit is the 24 h watch timeout (Task was processing for more than 4d 12h 13m 35s #2182).\\nThe Our system stuck for long, and didn't announce ready to merge commit in multiple cases #4048 stuck-CI monitor skips this case on purpose. findGhostQueuedRuns keeps only status === 'queued'. In createStuckCiMonitor.onPendingWorkflowRuns, ghostRuns.length === 0 resets the streak and returns, so the \\\"CI wait stuck\\\" PR notice is never posted for pending / waiting runs. (The run used 2.39.14, which is older than Our system stuck for long, and didn't announce ready to merge commit in multiple cases #4048. Current main 2.43.3 still has the same gap.)\\nThe Telegram monitor knows nothing about the watch phase of /solve. /fix has phase markers (src/fix-progress.lib.mjs, [HIVE-MIND FIX], waiting-for-ci). /solve prints no comparable marker for \\\"AI finished, now monitoring PR, blocked by X since T\\\", so formatExecutingWorkSessionMessage keeps showing ⏳ Executing....\\nThe \\\"working session is ended\\\" comment is misleading. It is posted before startAutoRestartUntilMergeable (on by default: 'auto-restart-until-mergeable' default: true in src/solve.config.lib.mjs), so the operator thinks the task is done or hung while it is actually polling.\\n\\nMissing diagnostics (a bug in its own right)\\nThe logs were just enough to find the cause, and only because log B (the start-command stdout capture) happened to contain the whole watch loop. Specific gaps:\\n\\nThe solve log file covering the 5 h was never uploaded. Log A is a snapshot taken at 00:34:48. The interrupted-session upload at 06:13:19 was SIGKILLed after about 10 s, while it was still sanitizing 114 MB (the first upload of 113 MB took 34 min). Only the timestamp-less stdout capture survived.\\nNo timestamps in the evidence that survived. In log B, solve's lines have no ISO timestamps, and the watch loop prints only a local h:mm:ss AM without date or timezone (🔍 Check #N: 6:13:18 AM). Timing had to be rebuilt from check numbers and the 120 s interval.\\nNo age, job count or cause for the blocking run. The line is just &lt;workflow W&gt; [pending]. It should say pending for 3h28m, 0 jobs, created 21:42Z, concurrency group busy (N other runs ahead).\"},{\"span\":[16730,20345],\"status\":\"unbound\",\"text\":\"Then the cause would be obvious on check Use https://www.wikifunctions.org as public AI skills #1.\\nNo escalation. 135 identical checks produced 135 identical blocks and no \\\"stuck\\\" log line, no PR comment and no Telegram update.\\nNo heartbeat during the 34 min sanitize + upload (00:34:48 → 01:08:40). There was one line, Streamed sanitize: … 114 block(s), and no progress such as block i/114, bytes uploaded, chunk 1/2, elapsed time.\\nKill notice without the pending operation. The notice reported memory, heap, disk and cgroup readings, but not the phase (watch_until_mergeable), the current blocker, the check number or the last heartbeat. It also said cause unknown for an operator /stop.\\nNoise: the full issue JSON ({\\\"body\\\": …}) is printed to stdout on every check. checkForIssueMetadataChanges(…, $, …) in the loop gets the mirroring $, not quietProbe($). That is 134 copies of the issue body in log B.\\n\\nProposed fixes\\n\\nClassify every non-completed HEAD run in getMergeBlockers / createStuckCiMonitor. Use status (queued / pending / waiting / action_required / in_progress), the job count (getWorkflowRunJobsCount) and the age. Handle pending + 0 jobs (concurrency queue) and waiting / action_required (approval) as their own cases, not as \\\"CI still running\\\".\\nBounded wait for runs that have not started. If all check runs passed, mergeStateStatus is CLEAN, and the only blockers are HEAD runs that never started (0 jobs) for longer than a threshold (for example HIVE_MIND_STUCK_PENDING_RUN_MINUTES, default 30–60 min), then:\\n\\npost the \\\"CI wait stuck\\\" PR notice (extend buildStuckCiNoticeComment with \\\"held by concurrency group, N runs ahead\\\");\\nafter a second, configurable limit (for example 2 h, well under 24 h), end the loop with an explicit decision and stop reason (reason: 'ci_not_started' via reportAutomationStop), or post \\\"ready to merge (workflow W has not started: concurrency queue)\\\" according to a documented policy;\\nnever cancel or re-run a pending run held by a concurrency group (that would lose its place in the queue). The Our system stuck for long, and didn't announce ready to merge commit in multiple cases #4048 cancel + re-run path must stay limited to ghost queued runs.\\n\\n\\nPhase markers and a Telegram status for /solve, like /fix. For example, [HIVE-MIND SOLVE] {\\\"phase\\\":\\\"watch\\\",\\\"blocker\\\":\\\"ci_pending\\\",\\\"detail\\\":\\\"workflow W pending 0 jobs\\\",\\\"since\\\":\\\"…\\\",\\\"check\\\":87,\\\"deadline\\\":\\\"…\\\"} emitted on every check, and the session monitor shows it instead of ⏳ Executing.... The status should refresh at least every 5–10 min, even when nothing changes, so a frozen status means a frozen process.\\nHeartbeat + watchdog for every wait after the final log (log sanitize/upload, cooldown, the CI loop, gh calls, child processes). Each wait has a name, a start time, a deadline and a heartbeat line with an ISO timestamp. A watchdog that sees no heartbeat for X min logs the pending operation and makes the finish / auto-continue / auto-resume decision itself, so the decision never depends on an operator.\\nHonest end-of-session comment. If monitoring continues after the solution log is posted, the comment says so (\\\"AI session ended; now monitoring PR until mergeable, timeout …\\\"). When monitoring ends, a final short comment gives the decision and the reason.\\n/stop and log upload. Give the interrupt handler enough grace before SIGKILL to finish (or at least start) the upload, or upload only the tail since the last uploaded snapshot (log A had already uploaded the first 113 MB). Stop the watch loop before starting the upload (parkIfShuttingDown covers new checks in 2.43.x;\"},{\"span\":[20346,24262],\"status\":\"unbound\",\"text\":\"also cancel the in-flight check). Attribute the exit to the operator so the notice says \\\"Stopped by operator via /stop\\\" and not cause unknown (No log uploaded on stop #2052).\\nKill notice / $ --status diagnostics: include the last phase marker (phase, blocker, check number, since, deadline) and the last heartbeat time.\\nLogging: ISO timestamps on the watch-loop lines in stdout (or a timestamped stdout capture). Use quietProbe($) for checkForIssueMetadataChanges so the issue JSON is not printed every 2 min. Add sanitize/upload progress lines (block i/N, chunk k/M, elapsed).\\n\\nAcceptance criteria\\n\\n A regression test with a HEAD workflow run in status: pending, 0 jobs, created 4 h ago, all check runs passed and mergeStateStatus: CLEAN. The watch loop logs the run as \\\"not started (concurrency queue / pending), age, 0 jobs\\\" on the first check, posts one PR notice after the threshold, and ends with an explicit, reported decision within the configured limit (not 24 h). It never cancels or re-runs the pending run.\\n The same test passes for status: waiting and action_required (approval-gated runs), with a message that says approval is needed.\\n During the watch phase, the Telegram message for a /solve session shows the phase, the blocker, the time since it started and the deadline, and is refreshed at least every 10 min. ⏳ Executing... is shown only while the AI tool is running.\\n Every wait after the final solution log has a deadline and a heartbeat. A test with a fake wait that never ends shows that the watchdog logs the pending operation and makes the finish / continue / resume decision on its own.\\n The end-of-session PR comment does not say \\\"working session is ended\\\" while monitoring goes on. A final decision comment is posted when monitoring ends.\\n /stop during the watch loop: the loop stops before the upload starts, the interrupted-session log (or its tail since the last upload) is attached, and the kill / stop notice says \\\"stopped by operator\\\" with the last phase and blocker. It does not say SIGKILL; cause unknown.\\n Watch-loop lines in stdout have ISO-8601 UTC timestamps, and the issue JSON is no longer printed on every check.\\n A test for a 100+ MB log upload checks that progress lines appear at least every 60 s.\\n\\nEnvironment\\n\\nhive-mind 2.39.14 (solve), Docker isolation (konard/hive-mind-dind), Node 26. The source references above are from main @ 2.43.3, where the pending-run gap still exists.\\nTool: Claude Code, claude-opus-5-5 (+ claude-sonnet-5-5 sub-agents), --think high; 15 sub-sessions, 12 sub-agent calls.\\nFlags: --think high --tool claude --attach-logs --verbose --no-tool-check --disable-report-issue --language en. --auto-restart-until-mergeable was on through its default, not passed explicitly.\\n--on-session-kill=resume.\\nThe full logs are in a private repository and are available to maintainers on request.\\nActivitySign up for free to join this conversation on GitHub. Already have an account? Sign in to commentMetadataMetadataAssigneesNo one assignedLabelsNo labelsNo labelsTypeNo typeProjectsNo projectsMilestoneNo milestoneRelationshipsNone yetDevelopmentNo branches or pull requestsIssue actionsOpen in GitHub Copilot app\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n\\n\\n\\n    \\n  \\n\\n  \\n\\n  \\n            \\n  Footer\\n\\n  \\n\\n\\n  \\n    \\n      \\n        \\n    \\n\\n\\n      \\n        &copy; 2026 GitHub,&nbsp;Inc.\\n      \\n    \\n\\n    \\n      Footer navigation\\n\\n      \\n\\n\\n          \\n            Terms\\n          \\n\\n          \\n            Privacy\\n          \\n\\n\\n            \\n              Security\\n            